<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29892" root="عقد" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُعَقَدٌ</span></b>  [<i>Tied in many knots</i>]. One says <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خُيُوطٌ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُعَقَّدَةٌ</span> [<i>Threads,</i> or <i>strings, tied in many knots</i>]:
the latter word being with teshdeed to denote
muchness, or multiplicity. (S, O, L.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And
[hence] applied to language, (S, O, L, K,) as
meaning <i>Rendered obscure:</i> (S, O, L:) or [simply] <i>obscure.</i> (K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَعْقُودٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b4-  And
see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَقِيد</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b5-  It also occurs in a trad. as meaning
<i>A sort of</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بُرْد</span>, <i>of the manufacture of Hejer.</i> (L.)

